{"title":"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Rearrangement)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Rearrangement)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution:_Only_basic_rules_of_exponents_are_needed\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution: Only basic rules of exponents are needed</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive real numbers, then\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb94a39e3190f57fcbb1f2fbe849a6c038b66e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c\\ge (abc)^{(a+b+c)/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a43f70393f1230504c3240e9bfb86f22915f96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x\\ln{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fde8d2440e4cba923ffacebd472fd080c02d76ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;&#39;(x)=\\frac{1}{x}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />; therefore, it is a convex function and we can apply <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jensen%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Jensen&#39;s Inequality\">Jensen's Inequality</a>:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db0d87edcf1329bb08f89821fd547f050f23f363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\ln{a}+b\\ln{b}+c\\ln{c}}{3}\\ge \\left(\\frac{a+b+c}{3}\\right)\\ln\\left(\\frac{a+b+c}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"404\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>Apply <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a> to get\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872ec383ca01e8997916c1dbaee116fee66f8130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b+c}{3}\\ge \\sqrt[3]{abc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"139\" height=\"37\" /></center>\n<p>which implies\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da34b15dd7c8d75509c763b00ecc8f379c8cbd22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\ln{a}+b\\ln{b}+c\\ln{c}}{3}\\ge \\left(\\frac{a+b+c}{3}\\right)\\ln\\left(\\sqrt[3]{abc}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"367\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>Rearranging,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f59079c18ed4396607cf01df15d21c4dcb3d272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ln{a}+b\\ln{b}+c\\ln{c}\\ge\\left(\\frac{a+b+c}{3}\\right)\\ln\\left(abc\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"342\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3d10910bf66521a4c8e162549eec9efeb43285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = e^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> is an increasing function, we can conclude that:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635872e58e16d76df675269c7674dff286ad4dd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{a\\ln{a}+b\\ln{b}+c\\ln{c}}\\ge{e}^{\\ln\\left(abc\\right)(a+b+c)/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>which simplifies to the desired inequality.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f7efac9dbe06df4ab041f71ce1f1fa5ace5b52b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^ab^bc^c)(a^bb^cc^a)(a^cb^ac^b)=\\left((abc)^{(a+b+c)/3}\\right)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"332\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>So if we can prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9f9aef004e45daad6cce947356347c95afb54e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c\\ge a^bb^cc^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d094cdf999b5e076723fb95cf24112d5fc53ce9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c\\ge a^cb^ac^b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />, then we are done.\n</p><p>WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65232ade0c0280ce3a076bc0e68db36a5f2269d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ge b\\ge c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c8caeb092d395425f75066a5361e9c42018fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^ab^bc^c)\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{c}{a}\\right)^{a-b}\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{c}{b}\\right)^{b-c}=a^bb^cc^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"272\" height=\"37\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f2cbd5fb0f241fb162ed27b221d0453def35fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{c}{a} \\le  1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9fc7caa1a663f31a9d23da19e68f6cf050df6d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{c}{b} \\le  1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f819964dbaa7b63e4d4b75d1a2d4dce4d0b77baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7b4262bdb9790baaa1c0ba7f5739fcc413dffe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-c \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e122afa2069ef2935843fd49b42052e712caa342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c \\ge a^bb^cc^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921567b62ccce4de9503a0e7d2182855c1e4d35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^ab^bc^c)\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{b}{a}\\right)^{a-b}\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{c}{a}\\right)^{b-c}=a^cb^ac^b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"279\" height=\"47\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d86fd1e4f4d1b73b0a1f91f099efa7ee08a82b56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{b}{a} \\le  1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f2cbd5fb0f241fb162ed27b221d0453def35fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{c}{a} \\le  1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f819964dbaa7b63e4d4b75d1a2d4dce4d0b77baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7b4262bdb9790baaa1c0ba7f5739fcc413dffe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-c \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3ab0a0fc859b993fd2b665fdce11a9eb869b46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c \\ge a^cb^ac^b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81cbe7f856ab9874bf221575de351aa1d515fd6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^ab^bc^c)^3\\ge (a^ab^bc^c)(a^bb^cc^a)(a^cb^ac^b)=\\left((abc)^{(a+b+c)/3}\\right)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"425\" height=\"26\" />, and cube-rooting both sides gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb94a39e3190f57fcbb1f2fbe849a6c038b66e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c\\ge (abc)^{(a+b+c)/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" /> as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65232ade0c0280ce3a076bc0e68db36a5f2269d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ge b\\ge c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a89ba4bccbd2829b0a58554976cb619cde9eccd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = ax$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8fe88b1b6ab5c722ecc992817ade0377c3b2051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = ay$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f6ccc7a2d5fab315122e2fb75fd4e2927ab4a29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/2099af869d8ee475858c2645af3dd7b5e6ee6a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We want to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/90710de778bc08a16db3215e68541daeb5e2cbb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a)^{a}(ax)^{ax}(ay)^{ay} \\ge (a \\cdot ax \\cdot ay)^{\\frac{a + ax + ay}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"295\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Simplifying and combining terms on each side, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e4933ef72b81825eb883c0403ea161e04f48a98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{a + ax + ay}x^{ax}y^{ay} \\ge a^{a + ax + ay}(xy)^{\\frac{a + ax + ay}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"295\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, we can divide out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8c1be07ae7ad1d91cb3abc9535687a17ea4e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{a + ax + ay}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1efde29d34b3b20c7ddcc69332423146629bbfbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{ax}y^{ay} \\ge (xy)^{\\frac{a + ax + ay}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Take the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />th root of each side and then cube both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a97508d4db5a91a07220b60af03d7e294de112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{3x}y^{3y} \\ge (xy)^{1 + x + y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7bad4e1088a244ff7dbd8fc6df3a4c9c968dd3b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2x-1}y^{2y-1} \\ge x^{y}y^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67ea16319f9931b4076579a59a7134fa663cbec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x - 1 \\ge x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b644ea8c969194bb5fdec8f8f547962c033923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y - 1 \\ge y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, we only need to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d707f2ec599eef575d28b6e060fb3153da2aa64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{x}y^{y} \\ge x^{y}y^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> for our given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13f250f1481908fb7f400238ab1c0c2b04d8c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\ge x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e320015783a0e5bbfc2b10cedee26582164e456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y =kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/172e6dadffd9800e796f3f96a1e24ce2a1840f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Then our expression becomes \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51d31eafc1835062c29beaa46c122c637e1e2a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{x}(xk)^{xk} \\ge x^{xk}(xk)^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56c6134af542ec52cd76f12b580b94c21b00516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{x+xk}k^{xk} \\ge x^{x+xk}k^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be11479cdf8d1158585790610b745807eeffe62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{xk} \\ge k^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/017cc38e6c5858c1861bb8cb3bedc064c604c59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^k \\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This is clearly true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/172e6dadffd9800e796f3f96a1e24ce2a1840f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65232ade0c0280ce3a076bc0e68db36a5f2269d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ge b\\ge c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. Then sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> majorizes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495c6c8b23d9a12e4a4bf77e9d8b1815d9f39851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{a+b+c}{3},\\frac{a+b+c}{3},\\frac{a+b+c}{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"250\" height=\"37\" />. Thus by Muirhead's Inequality, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc52bf5bb74b857fd8c40ff2e09cf81fa461315d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{sym} a^ab^bc^c \\ge \\sum_{sym} a^{\\frac{a+b+c}{3}}b^{\\frac{a+b+c}{3}}c^{\\frac{a+b+c}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"268\" height=\"41\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69b7c30190a5f1f82f35e3ca27bc269ed8d0cccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c \\ge (abc)^{\\frac{a+b+c}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88c67319518b59ca26063ecf9232b171e4df2d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt[3]{abc}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"83\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e013ea48881ccd82ab3fc43b6388578f894cd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{b}{\\sqrt[3]{abc}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"81\" height=\"44\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e1e9747ce5f53456d041a1b8dbd6050e01c555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac{c}{\\sqrt[3]{abc}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4e962c8ab321be15667f8986436dc8f4e42c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> and a straightforward calculation reduces the problem to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d20872118974858368536c1b642c29048a02a27.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^xy^yz^z \\ge 1.\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />\nWLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f5707adcc65bde988863514ff1789e024bec60a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge y\\ge z.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fddb63cb1b715bf1c66330657b961abf54d6437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef11834f5030fea9f07e770df81295d2b704b11c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff4c486d2597ee76dbed66fcb588021e2a784a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=\\frac{1}{z} \\ge 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06ff9be02ec9d5a027fa835f3b10a5be865265c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^xy^yz^z=x^{x-y}(xy)^{y-z}(xyz)^z \\ge 1.\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>J.Z.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Cubing both sides of the given inequality gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03e17aa37fb8652ecfdd72edcd8a58884d8fb80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^{3a}b^{3b}c^{3c}\\ge(abc)^{a+b+c}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />\nIf we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2961d02fc0a65b37ba6d7be33e0343cdaf8e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{3a}b^{3b}c^{3c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" /> as the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1cb96a3344461b85f9e6eb91850987abd720a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />'s, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f55180c90b5e279d1cea00eee6163532dee3e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />'s, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/61184eee486e1df90e7fb87eea1a1ba70f60d5a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3c$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5ba00aad5790d10d1c906522a49ec5277f999e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;s$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we get that \n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4215e8bd630d3d7865850e3474be47fb991464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3(a+b+c)]{a^{3a}b^{3b}c^{3c}}\\ge\\frac{3(a+b+c)}{\\frac{3a}{a}+\\frac{3b}{b}+\\frac{3c}{c}}=\\frac{a+b+c}{3}\\ge\\sqrt[3]{abc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"412\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>by GM-HM, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d0d7039a400779d0c3013db5ed5a4950068462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dcceb5127d10665924b2e5b1f32de1cd53d8fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bk$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a637bd5b10089814eaef093703042a7e6a3f975d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ck$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, for some positive real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4c2f3d1d00d84d3ce9b11996f4121f30a4a6e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{ak}k^{ak}b^{bk}k^{bk}c^{ck}k^{ck} = a^{ak}b^{bk}c^{ck}k^{ak+bk+ck} \\ge {k^3abc}^{{ak+bk+ck}/3} = k^{ak+bk+ck}{abc}^{{ak+bk+ck}/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"646\" height=\"22\" />\nThis means that this inequality is homogeneous since both sides have the same power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> as a factor. Since the inequality is homogeneous, we can scale <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> so that their product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e32cfd3a6f5f31f73d0b272a5f7b1638fd16551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. This makes the inequality turn into something much more nicer to deal with. Now we have to prove:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1bfa64139bf3516461607f27b43bb552df0ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e32cfd3a6f5f31f73d0b272a5f7b1638fd16551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />.\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb89fb42d6a123bbb625282a0f12be47f54a0bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^a \\ge a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> even if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be54e826b0de7b5fbcefdd03fa87658ef6247c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb89fb42d6a123bbb625282a0f12be47f54a0bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^a \\ge a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fe3c1a72478575a4aa444b0b16c487007548da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^b \\ge b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f5c25be74b19875ac31d3956a75ba09a5712b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^c \\ge c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />. Multiplying these together we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3063055285a68a1a4e9ab2db8b08a44c8f7931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c \\ge abc = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />. This proves the desired result. Equality holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8dfa0e69992284ec2f621b4c356a3edbf99c9f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Rearrangement.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Rearrangement)\">Solution 8 (Rearrangement)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Rearrangement)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6dba60281698ebf018a03c7482e0d651cf03a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2a=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/3531359de52d6a1ac68f30c3c20f6a1789b2a27e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2b=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59cb20a4f02dcf93377839366ac7d6a5b113ff8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2c=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" />, and WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d62d7246d542eaf5115aafb0703db5cecc5df29f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ge b\\ge c &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. \nThen we have both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65232ade0c0280ce3a076bc0e68db36a5f2269d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ge b\\ge c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cdefb24c29b899f42370d3eb21154dc387e38bcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge y \\ge z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.\nBy the rearrangement inequality, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356c6313663bdd2d0a7d0c2907da3a77c8a8613a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by+cz\\ge ay + bz +cx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"222\" height=\"16\" /> and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a8747a5e09d8ba474e043dbef3f8f6ca2a9b9c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by +cz\\ge az+bx+cy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" />.\nSumming, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f651423504bc3e50d833aac882e7f234520be8ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(ax+by+cz)\\ge a(y+z)+b(x+z)+c(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\nAdding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b3551ef942c5fc8cb3f101ae66b2b3022f59ef58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by+cz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />,we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01b030945ba420ae3f90c1fc1cc5534c673680f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by+cz\\ge \\frac{(a+b+c)(x+y+z)}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"297\" height=\"38\" />.\nNow we substitute back for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d648e4e251400761bed65aa91db7bad3c726031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2a^ab^bc^c\\ge \\log_2(abc)^{\\frac{a+b+c}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"212\" height=\"23\" />.\nRaising <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the power of each side, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fae375e864afa563130747c48b1400921658498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c\\ge (abc)^{\\frac{a+b+c}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume without loss of generality that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57c4f96dc49aa339e443ef0b7d16f9ce178cf84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\le b\\le c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. Then, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2106108a07c3779aaec70c2ec4a398688f79a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b/a\\ge 1, c/a\\ge 1, c/b\\ge 1, b-a\\ge 0, c-a\\ge 0, c-b\\ge 0.\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"18\" />\nIt follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7fec67272e329450fa08750eebcdd0e3502d422.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(b/a)^{(b-a)/3}\\cdot (c/a)^{(c-a)/3}\\cdot (c/b)^{(c-b)/3}\\ge 1.\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"20\" />\nWe can \"distribute\" the exponents, which gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c8380871ca3d2532345d2d2c3d53a326db6ff98c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{b^{(b-a)/3}}{a^{(b-a)/3}}\\cdot \\dfrac{c^{(c-a)/3}}{a^{(c-a)/3}}\\cdot \\dfrac{c^{(c-b)/3}}{b^{(c-b)/3}}\\ge 1.\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"40\" />\nNotice that in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fac10183d80396d31df1789a100066ccdd1d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{(c-b)/3}$\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> in the denominator of the third fraction can be brought out of the denominator by negating its exponent. This gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d5f1f2f8cd8a2f873ed02400bb0345d769672a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{b^{(b-a)/3}}{a^{(b-a)/3}}\\cdot \\dfrac{c^{(c-a)/3}}{a^{(c-a)/3}}\\cdot c^{(c-b)/3} \\cdot b^{(b-c)/3}\\ge 1.\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"40\" />\nWe can move around terms on the left to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac3a77cd32b1e904e6024606073f2d2945faca61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\dfrac{b^{(b-a)/3}\\cdot b^{(b-c)/3}}{a^{(b-a)/3}}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{c^{(c-a)/3}\\cdot c^{(c-b)/3}}{a^{(c-a)/3}}\\right)\\ge 1.\\]\" width=\"344\" height=\"45\" />\nNow we combine the exponents in the numerators. This gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630f9af1dd17e98fb8ffb46942c212e93c76f5d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\dfrac{b^{(2b-c-a)/3}}{a^{(b-a)/3}}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{c^{(2c-b-a)/3}}{a^{(c-a)/3}}\\right)\\ge 1.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"44\" />\nWe multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64b7dc590c59b5fd3c4788920d99f167100f2aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(a^{(b-a)/3}\\right)\\left(a^{(c-a)/3}\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"158\" height=\"22\" /> which gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24e6739e3afcdeeb9fac31be273df84a415e664.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(b^{(2b-c-a)/3}\\right)\\left(c^{(2c-b-a)/3}\\right)\\ge \\left(a^{(b-a)/3}\\right)\\left(a^{(c-a)/3}\\right).\\]\" width=\"372\" height=\"22\" />\nWe then multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d2f0fd8c1594ff3aa1eb12a5e442a41cfbb3a59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(b^{(c-a)/3}\\right)\\left(c^{(b-a)/3}\\right):$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"156\" height=\"22\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe78dce359eddacf160e64e052009cb27bc75841.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(b^{(2b-2a)/3}\\right)\\left(c^{(2c-2a)/3}\\right)\\ge \\left(a^{(b-a)/3}\\right)\\left(c^{(b-a)/3}\\right)\\left(a^{(c-a)/3}\\right)\\left(b^{(c-a)/3}\\right).\\]\" width=\"503\" height=\"22\" />\nMultiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63cc4822c45dbee700b0e16dea90f60202459678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(b^{(b-a)/3}\\right)\\left(c^{(c-a)/3}\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"154\" height=\"22\" /> then simplifying both sides with exponent laws, gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/059fe76d783672602263e34e854c0aa0d5ed7569.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^{b-a}\\cdot c^{c-a}\\ge (abc)^{(b+c-2a)/3}.\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />\nFinally, we multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158e8a9798e0d07eadb35859fbd2678a2b602dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(abc)^a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> Combining exponents one last time gives the desired\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f28502169867bedcb9c8b7d288ce475ec96116b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^a b^b c^c\\ge (abc)^{(a+b+c)/3}.\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />\n--MenuThreeOne\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10\">Solution 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 2:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7665cf39e7691d096c423516237b20b245140fd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^ab^bc^c \\cdot a^bb^cc^a \\cdot a^cb^ac^b = (abc)^{(\\frac{a+b+c}{3})^3}\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>We show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c31a19631c14fc5d3a671b15e599bcef740791.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^ab^bc^c \\ge a^bb^cc^a\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e745979d93cbc8397d05e1a906132c2d87073b4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^ab^bc^c \\ge a^cb^ac^b\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>By definition, the first inequality is trivial via the Rearrangement Inequality:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c258af384cf8a0cd95673fc01697a96758933a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\ln(a)+b\\ln(b)+c\\ln(c) \\ge b\\ln(a) + c\\ln(b) + a\\ln(c)\\]\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, the second:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb940db47931918c408bdb158adf5cac91701867.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\ln(a)+b\\ln(b)+c\\ln(c) \\ge c\\ln(a) + a\\ln(b) + b\\ln(c)\\]\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Hence the two results are proved. As in solution 2:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef27547c010d9bb6a4e022bd01277cec1cca542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^ab^bc^c)^3\\ge (a^ab^bc^c)(a^bb^cc^a)(a^cb^ac^b)=\\left((abc)^{(a+b+c)/3}\\right)^3\\]\" width=\"424\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>and through cube roots the result <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb94a39e3190f57fcbb1f2fbe849a6c038b66e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^ab^bc^c\\ge (abc)^{(a+b+c)/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" /> is obtained.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution:_Only_basic_rules_of_exponents_are_needed\">Video Solution: Only basic rules of exponents are needed</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution: Only basic rules of exponents are needed\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/lXmUugsPb1U?si=JAp8PJ5DxnULtUTB\">https://youtu.be/lXmUugsPb1U?si=JAp8PJ5DxnULtUTB</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO\" title=\"1974 USAMO\">1974 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1974\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1974 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/viewtopic.php?t=102633\">Simple Olympiad Inequality</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/viewtopic.php?t=98846\">Hard inequality</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/viewtopic.php?t=85663\">Inequality</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=82706\">Some q's on usamo write ups</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/viewtopic.php?t=213258\">ineq</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=46247\">exponents (generalization)</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017001049\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.072 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.101 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 776/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1617/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27193/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.807      1 -total\n 34.63%    6.512      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 32.39%    6.091      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 31.63%    5.948      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7529:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017001049 and revision id 286398. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}